[40.265787, "o", "PASSAGE_0000: Uses\r\ntemporarily relieves these symptoms due to hay fever or other upper respiratory allergies:\r\n- runny nose\r\n- sneezing\r\n- itchy, watery eyes\r\n- itching of the nose or throat\r\nPASSAGE_0001: Do not use if you have ever had an allergic reaction to this product or any of its ingredients.\r\nPASSAGE_0002: Ask a doctor before use if you have kidney disease.  Your doctor should determine if you need a different dose.\r\nPASSAGE_0003: - do not take more than directed\r\n- do not take at the same time as aluminum or magnesium antacids\r\n- do not take with fruit juices\r\nPASSAGE_0004: Stop use and ask a doctor if an allergic reaction to this product occurs.  Seek medical help right away.\r\nPASSAGE_0005: If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a health professional before use.\r\nPASSAGE_0006: Keep out of reach of children. In case of overdose, get medical help or contact a Poison Control Center right away (1-800-222-1222).\r\nPASSAGE_0007: adults and children 12 years of age and over take one 60 mg tablet with water every 12 hours; do not take more than 2 tablets in 24 hours\r\nPASSAGE_0008: do not use\r\nadults 65 years of age and older\r\nPASSAGE_0009: - store between 20-25°C (68-77°F)\r\n- protect from excessive moisture\r\n- retain carton for complete product information and warnings\r\nPASSAGE_0010: colloidal silicon dioxide, croscarmellose sodium, hypromellose, iron oxide black, iron oxide red, iron oxide yellow, lactose monohydrate, macrogol, magnesium stearate, microcrystalline cellulose, pregelatinized starch, titanium dioxide\r\nPASSAGE_0011: Antihistamine\r\nIndoor/Outdoor Relief of:\r\nPASSAGE_0012: Actual Size\r\nCOMPARE TO ALLEGRA® 12 HOUR ALLERGY active ingredient*\r\n"]
